      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ x & =2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({315}^{\u2218}) \\\\ x & =2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta  \\\\ y & =2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({315}^{\u2218}) \\\\ y & =2\\cdot -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ y & =-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(\\sqrt{2},-\\sqrt{2}).$"
    },
